/* ============================== PHASE 1 ==============================
   Crypto & Encryption Engine — source: erp_crypto_utils.js (unmodified)
   ======================================================================= */
/* =========================================================================
   ERP CRYPTO & SECURITY UTILITY MODULE — Phase 1
   =========================================================================
   Self-contained. No external libraries. Everything runs on the browser's
   built-in Web Crypto API (window.crypto.subtle), the same engine already
   used elsewhere in this ERP for password hashing (sha256Hex / PBKDF2).

   Why Web Crypto instead of a hand-rolled "pure JS" AES/RSA:
   - It's already present in every modern browser — zero extra bytes to
     ship, zero supply-chain risk from a third-party crypto library.
   - Hand-rolled JS AES/RSA implementations are exactly the kind of code
     that quietly gets timing side-channels or padding bugs wrong. The
     browser's implementation is audited, hardware-accelerated, and is
     what "lightweight pure JS equivalent" should mean in practice: no
     dependency, not "reimplement AES by hand."

   Provides:
     - AES-256-GCM  symmetric encrypt/decrypt (passphrase-based)
     - RSA-OAEP     asymmetric encrypt/decrypt (keypair-based)
     - SHA-256 / PBKDF2 hashing for checksums, license keys, auth payloads
     - A safe localStorage/window.storage wrapper that transparently
       encrypts on write and decrypts on read

   Public API (as requested):
     encryptData(plaintext, passphrase)        -> Promise<string>
     decryptData(encryptedString, passphrase)  -> Promise<string>
     generateHash(data)                        -> Promise<string>

